[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "London System"]
[Variation "Queen's Pawn Game: Accelerated London System, 2...e6"]
[ECO "D00"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "b2-pressure,transposition"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "1...d5 2.Bf4 e6"]
[Start "london-bf4-first 2.Bf4"]

2... e6 { Supports d5 and opens the bishop on f8, but the bishop on c8 is now shut in behind the pawn on e6. }
3. e3 { The usual pawn chain. Black's c8 bishop is shut in, so there is no ...Bf5 to think about. }
3... c5
( 3... Nf6 { Transposes to 2...Nf6 3.e3 e6. } )
( 3... Nc6 { Transposes to 2...Nc6 3.e3 e6. } )
( 3... Bd6 4. Bg3 { Keeps the bishop. If Black takes on g3, hxg3 opens the h-file for White's rook. } 4... Nf6 ( 4... c5 5. c3 Nc6 6. Nd2 ) ( 4... f5 5. c4 ) 5. Nd2 { Transposes to 2...Nf6 3.e3 e6 4.Nd2 Bd6 5.Bg3. } )
( 3... f5 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. Bd3 { Aims at the pawn on f5 and the kingside. The e5 square, weakened by ...f5, is a home for a knight later. } )
( 3... Bb4+ 4. c3 { Asks the bishop where it is going. It has to go back, and Black has lost a move. } 4... Bd6 5. Bg3 )
( 3... c6 4. Nd2 )
4. c3 { Backs up d4, so if Black takes there a pawn recaptures and the centre holds. If ...Qb6 comes, the queen can meet it on b3. }
4... Nc6
( 4... Nf6 5. Nd2 { Transposes to 2...Nf6 3.e3 e6 4.Nd2 c5 5.c3. } )
( 4... Qb6 5. Qb3 { Offers a queen trade, which takes away the piece hitting b2. } 5... Nc6 6. Nd2 )
( 4... cxd4 5. exd4 { Recaptures towards the centre. The e-file opens and the bishop on f1 can go to d3 at once. } )
( 4... Bd6 5. Bxd6 Qxd6 6. Nd2 )
5. Nd2
5... Nf6 { Transposes to the main line, 2...Nf6 3.e3 e6 4.Nd2 c5 5.c3 Nc6. }
( 5... Bd6 6. Bg3 )
( 5... cxd4 6. exd4 ) *
